+/* Markup pointers.
+ *
+ * A markup pointer sits between the tokens of a document: the begin tag and the end tag of an
+ * element are a token each, and so is every character of text. It is kept as a collapsed DOM
+ * range, so the engine moves it along when the document changes. The positions "after the
+ * last character of a text node" and "after the text node" are one markup position, so they
+ * are compared after being moved out of the text node. */
